    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d59">

                <pb facs="0192" n="84" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg84"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/8361: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-03-08T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 8, 1927—4
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 8—9:20
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>200. Regarding commander in chief’s telegram of March 7th to the chief of naval
                    operations, 0007–1800, concerning prevention of Chinese factions’ naval fighting
                    on the Whangpoo, I consider the Department’s 216, September 13, 4 p.m.,
                        1924,<anchor n="76" xml:id="d59-f1"/> applies and suggest that Admiral
                    Williams be instructed to cooperate with his foreign colleagues to that effect
                    and that I be authorized by telegraph to adopt this attitude should necessity
                    arise.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
